Presidential elections were held in [[Poland]] on 28 June 2020. As no candidate received a majority of the vote, a second round was held on 12 July, in which incumbent president [[Andrzej Duda]], running with the support of the incumbent government of the [[Law and Justice (Poland)|Law and Justice]] (PiS) party,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Strybel |first1=Robert |title=Poland to elect next president on June 28|url=http://ampoleagle.com/poland-to-elect-next-president-on-june-p14491-96.htm |agency=ampoleagle.com |date=10 June 2020}}</ref> faced off against [[Civic Platform]] vice-chairman and [[Mayor of Warsaw]] [[Rafał Trzaskowski]]. In the second round Duda was re-elected for a second term with 51% of the vote, becoming the first incumbent to win re-election since [[Aleksander Kwaśniewski]] in [[2000 Polish presidential election|2000]].

The first round of voting was due to be held on 10 May 2020, but was postponed due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic in Poland]]. On 6 May 2020 the [[Agreement (political party)|Agreement]] party, which was in a governing alliance with their senior alliance partner [[Law and Justice (Poland)|Law and Justice]] (PiS) party and was opposed to pursuing the original election date, reached an arrangement to set new dates for the election. The following day, the PKW declared that the election would not take place on 10 May 2020. On 3 June 2020, the [[Marshal of the Sejm]], [[Elżbieta Witek]], ordered the first round of the election to be held on 28 June 2020 and scheduled the second round on 12 July 2020.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Wybory prezydenckie odbędą się 28 czerwca - podała marszałek Sejmu|url=https://www.msn.com/pl-pl/wiadomosci/polska/wybory-prezydenckie-odb%C4%99d%C4%85-si%C4%99-28-czerwca-poda%C5%82a-marsza%C5%82ek-sejmu/ar-BB14XLmR?ocid=msedgntp|access-date=2020-06-03|website=msn.com}}</ref><ref name="TVN24_elections_date">{{cite news|date=2 June 2020|title=Marszałek Sejmu Elżbieta Witek podała termin wyborów prezydenckich|website=TVN24.pl|url=https://tvn24.pl/polska/wybory-prezydenckie-2020-nowy-termin-podany-przez-marszalek-sejmu-elzbiete-witek-4601061|quote=Marszałek Sejmu Elżbieta Witek poinformowała w środę, że wybory prezydenckie w 2020 roku odbędą się 28 czerwca.}}</ref>

{{TOC limit}}

Duda's victory marked the sixth national election in a row where the right-wing PiS party defeated the opposition centrist and center-left forces.<ref>{{cite news |title=A bitterly divided Poland narrowly reelects right-wing President Andrzej Duda |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/poland-andrzej-duda-bitterly-divided-polish-nation-narrowly-reelects-conservative-president/ |date=July 14, 2020|author1=Anna Noryskiewicz}}</ref>

==Electoral system==
The President of Poland is directly elected using a [[two-round system]] for a five-year term, with a two-term limit. [[Andrzej Duda]]'s first term expired on 6 August 2020 when he reaffirmed his oath of office before the [[National Assembly (Poland)|National Assembly]], a joint session of the [[Sejm]] and [[Senate of Poland|Senate]] and began his second term.

Pursuant to the provisions of the [[Constitution of Poland|Constitution]], the president must be elected by an absolute majority of valid votes. If no candidate succeeds in passing this threshold in the first round, a second round of voting is contested between with the two candidates who received the largest shares of the vote.

In order to be registered to contest the election, a candidate must be a Polish citizen, be at least 35 years old on the day of the first round of the election, and have collected at least 100,000 voters' signatures by 10 June 2020 at midnight.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Wybory 2020 - kalendarz wyborczy. Dwa dni na zgłoszenie komitetu, 100 tys. podpisów w tydzień|url=https://wiadomosci.gazeta.pl/wiadomosci/7,143907,25999332,wybory-2020-kalendarz-wyborczy-dwa-dni-na-zgloszenie-komitetu.html|access-date=2020-06-08|website=gazetapl|date=3 June 2020 |language=pl}}</ref>

Polls opened on election day at 07:00 [[Central European Summer Time|CEST]] and closed at 21:00 [[Central European Summer Time|CEST]] ([[Coordinated Universal Time|UTC]]+2).<ref name=":2">{{Cite web|url=https://wybory.gov.pl/prezydent20200628/|title=Wybory Prezydenta Rzeczypospolitej Polskiej w 2020 r.|website=wybory.gov.pl}}</ref>

==COVID-19, election timing and controversy==
{{see also|COVID-19 pandemic in Poland|Impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on politics}}
The election was originally scheduled for 10 May 2020, which caused extreme political controversy related to the COVID-19 pandemic. Many candidates,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.onet.pl/?srcc=ucs&pid=970a231f-9f46-4fa0-9dc0-8bd64f94fee5&sid=b177a2c9-166f-4113-9b28-185bbe554807|title=Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska: To nie jest czas na kampanię i wybory|date=23 March 2020|website=onet.pl (polish)|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220523221026/https://www.onet.pl/?srcc=ucs&pid=970a231f-9f46-4fa0-9dc0-8bd64f94fee5&sid=b177a2c9-166f-4113-9b28-185bbe554807|archive-date=23 May 2022|access-date=18 April 2020}}</ref> constitutionalists<ref>{{cite web|url=https://wyborcza.pl/7,75398,25799457,prof-chmaj-dzis-nie-da-sie-przeprowadzic-wyborow-bezpiecznych.html|title=Prof. Chmaj: Dziś nie da się przeprowadzić wyborów bezpiecznych dla obywateli|date=18 March 2020|website=wyborcza.pl (polish)|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200418200845/https://wyborcza.pl/7,75398,25799457,prof-chmaj-dzis-nie-da-sie-przeprowadzic-wyborow-bezpiecznych.html|archive-date=18 April 2020|access-date=18 April 2020}}</ref> and even politicians from the ruling coalition<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-health-coronavirus-poland-election/spat-over-presidential-election-tests-polands-ruling-coalition-idUSKBN21L0N7 |title=Spat over presidential election tests Poland's ruling coalition |author1=Anna Koper  |author2=Marcin Goclowski |date=3 April 2020 |publisher=[[Reuters]] |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20200418201256/https://www.reuters.com/article/us-health-coronavirus-poland-election/spat-over-presidential-election-tests-polands-ruling-coalition-idUSKBN21L0N7 |archive-date=18 April 2020 |access-date=18 April 2020}}</ref> criticized the government's plan of holding the election as originally scheduled during the pandemic. As a compromise, the [[Agreement (political party)|Agreement]] political party proposed lengthening the president's term by two years, which was supported by the [[Ministry of Health (Poland)|Minister of Health]], [[Łukasz Szumowski]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/kraj/wybory-prezydenckie-2020-szumowski-o-propozycji-gowina-bardzo-dobra/glwkyry|title=Szumowski o przedłużeniu kadencji prezydenta: bardzo dobra propozycja|date=2020-04-15|website=Onet Wiadomości|language=pl|access-date=2020-04-20}}</ref> This was rejected by the opposition. The main opposition party, [[Civic Platform]], wanted the election to be held in May 2021.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://tvn24.pl/wybory-prezydenckie-2020/wybory-prezydenckie-2020-borys-budka-i-koalicja-obywatelska-proponuje-nowy-termin-wyborow-4560384|title=Koalicja Obywatelska proponuje wybory prezydenckie za rok|website=TVN24|access-date=2020-04-20}}</ref> The ruling conservative party [[Law and Justice (Poland)|Law and Justice]] also wished to change the electoral rules<ref>{{cite web|url=https://oko.press/pis-pozbawil-uprawnien-pkw-hermelinski-to-wola-o-pomste-do-nieba/|title=PiS pozbawił uprawnień PKW. Hermeliński: "To woła o pomstę do nieba"|author1=Mariusz Jałoszewski |author2=Agata Szczęśniak|date=17 April 2020|website=oko.press (polish)|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200418201936/https://oko.press/pis-pozbawil-uprawnien-pkw-hermelinski-to-wola-o-pomste-do-nieba/|archive-date=18 April 2020|access-date=18 April 2020}}</ref> and to organize the election by postal voting only. Changing election rules less than six months prior to voting was ruled to be unconstitutional by the [[Constitutional Tribunal (Poland)|Constitutional Tribunal]] in 2011.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://dziennikustaw.gov.pl/DU/2011/s/149/889|title=Dziennik Ustaw 2011 r. nr 149, poz. 889|website=dziennikustaw.gov.pl}}</ref> Voting only by post is considered unconstitutional by some including Polish [[Supreme Court of Poland|Supreme Court]] in a non-binding opinion.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://sip.lex.pl/akty-prawne/dzu-dziennik-ustaw/kodeks-wyborczy-17679859|title=USTAWA z dnia 5 stycznia 2011 r. Kodeks wyborczy|date=31 March 2020|website=sip.lex.pl|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200418203531/https://sip.lex.pl/akty-prawne/dzu-dziennik-ustaw/kodeks-wyborczy-17679859|archive-date=18 April 2020|access-date=18 April 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.dziennikwschodni.pl/polityka/w-hermelinski-zmiany-w-kodeksie-wyborczym-mozna-wprowadzac-najpozniej-na-6-miesiecy-przed-wyborami,n,1000263466.html|title=W. Hermeliński: Zmiany w Kodeksie Wyborczym można wprowadzać najpóźniej na 6 miesięcy przed wyborami|date=29 March 2020|website=dziennikwschodni.pl|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200329170034/https://www.dziennikwschodni.pl/polityka/w-hermelinski-zmiany-w-kodeksie-wyborczym-mozna-wprowadzac-najpozniej-na-6-miesiecy-przed-wyborami,n,1000263466.html|archive-date=29 March 2020|access-date=18 April 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.senat.gov.pl/download/gfx/senat/pl/senatinicjatywypliki/8143/4/099_sn.pdf|title=Opinia Sądu Najwyższego na temat ustawy o szczególnych zasadach przeprowadzania wyborów powszechnych na Prezydenta Rzeczypospolitej Polskiej zarządzonych w 2020 r.|access-date=28 April 2020|archive-date=1 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201001173714/https://www.senat.gov.pl/download/gfx/senat/pl/senatinicjatywypliki/8143/4/099_sn.pdf|url-status=dead}}</ref>

===Email requests by Poczta Polska for private data===
At 02:26 early in the morning<ref name="dulkiewicz_news">{{cite news|title = (Tweet)|quote = O 2.26 przyszedł anonimowy e-mail o treści którą załączam poniżej. Składam zawiadomienie o możliwości popełnienia przestępstwa do prokuratury... Nie będę uczestniczyć w łamaniu prawa!|url = https://twitter.com/Dulkiewicz_A/status/1253285540625100800|date = 23 April 2020|website = Twitter|archive-url = https://archive.today/20200423195255/https://twitter.com/Dulkiewicz_A/status/1253285540625100800|url-status = live|archive-date = 23 April 2020|access-date = 23 April 2020}}</ref><ref name="sosnowiec_president_news">{{cite news|title = (Tweet)|quote = W środku nocy o godz. 2:26 otrzymaliśmy maila z podpisem "Poczta Polska" z wnioskiem o udostępnienie danych blisko 170 tys. Sosnowiczan. Zgłaszam sprawę do Prokuratory czy nie mamy do czynienia z próbą wyłudzenia danych osobowych.|url = https://twitter.com/ChecinskiPrez/status/1253281702266449920|date = 23 April 2020|website = Twitter|archive-url = https://archive.today/20200423195010/https://twitter.com/ChecinskiPrez/status/1253281702266449920|url-status = live|archive-date = 23 April 2020|access-date = 23 April 2020}}</ref> on 23 April, every Polish mayor and city council president<ref name="TVN24_news">{{cite news|title = "Od rana naradzamy się, co z tym zrobić", "kieruję sprawę do prokuratury". Samorządy o mailach od Poczty Polskiej|url = https://tvn24.pl/wybory-prezydenckie-2020/wybory-prezydenckie-2020-samorzady-o-mailach-od-poczty-polskiej-zapowiadaja-zawiadomienia-do-prokuratury-4563882|date = 23 April 2020|website = TVN24 (polish media)|archive-url = https://archive.today/20200423201507/https://tvn24.pl/wybory-prezydenckie-2020/wybory-prezydenckie-2020-samorzady-o-mailach-od-poczty-polskiej-zapowiadaja-zawiadomienia-do-prokuratury-4563882|url-status = live|archive-date = 23 April 2020|access-date = 23 April 2020}}</ref><ref name="jaskowiak_news">{{cite news|title = (Tweet)|quote = Jeżeli nadawcą tych maili, wysłanych o 2 w nocy do burmistrzów i prezydentów miast, rzeczywiście jest #PocztaPolska, a nie hakerzy próbujący wyłudzić dane milionów Polaków, to mówienie o państwie z tektury jest eufemizmem. To jest po prostu skandal!|url = https://twitter.com/jacek_jaskowiak/status/1253329834937212928/photo/1|date = 23 April 2020|website = Twitter|archive-url = https://archive.today/20200423203743/https://twitter.com/jacek_jaskowiak/status/1253329834937212928/photo/1|url-status = live|archive-date = 23 April 2020|access-date = 23 April 2020}}</ref> received an anonymous, unsigned<ref name="do_rzeczy">{{cite news|title = Truskolaski: Nie znam takiej osoby, która nazywałaby się Poczta Polska|url = https://dorzeczy.pl/kraj/137645/truskolaski-nie-znam-takiej-osoby-ktora-nazywalaby-sie-poczta-polska.html|date = 23 April 2020|website = Twitter|archive-url = https://archive.today/20200423203401/https://dorzeczy.pl/kraj/137645/truskolaski-nie-znam-takiej-osoby-ktora-nazywalaby-sie-poczta-polska.html|url-status = live|archive-date = 23 April 2020|access-date = 23 April 2020}}</ref> e-mail from [[Poczta Polska]] (Polish Post) saying that they were required to deliver the [[private data]] of 30 million Polish citizens including their [[PESEL]] (national identification number), date of birth, address, and other private data in a [[Text file|.txt]] file format lacking any passwords or security.<ref name="bezprawnik">{{cite news |title =Poczta Polska poprosiła gminy o listę nazwisk, adresów i numerów PESEL 30 milionów Polaków w plikach *.txt |url =https://bezprawnik.pl/poczta-polska-dane-osobowe-brak-podpisu/ |date =23 April 2020 |website =Twitter |archive-url =https://archive.today/20200423204412/https://bezprawnik.pl/wakacje-w-czasie-pandemii |url-status =live |archive-date =23 April 2020 |access-date =23 April 2020 }}</ref> Many Polish mayors and city council presidents,<ref name="ZMP_news">{{cite news|title = Komunikat ZMP|url = http://www.miasta.pl/aktualnosci/komunikat-zmp-a5678f5f-236a-4c2b-80d4-800876085530|date = 23 April 2020|website = Twitter|archive-url = https://archive.today/20200423200233/http://www.miasta.pl/aktualnosci/komunikat-zmp-a5678f5f-236a-4c2b-80d4-800876085530|url-status = live|archive-date = 23 April 2020|access-date = 23 April 2020}}</ref> lawyers, and other citizens<ref name="FB">{{cite news|title = Coraz rzadziej tu piszę o polityce i prawie, bo ludzie jedynie się wkurzają, przestają być dla siebie mili. Ale dziś warto....|url = https://www.facebook.com/aswalt/posts/10222148160041395|date = 23 April 2020|website = Twitter|archive-url = https://archive.today/20200423204022/https://www.facebook.com/aswalt/posts/10222148160041395|url-status = live|archive-date = 23 April 2020|access-date = 23 April 2020}}</ref> criticized the order to provide such private data, stating that the order violated the [[General Data Protection Regulation|GDPR]] and Polish Law, since the legal act referred to in the email had no legal validity; it concerned a bill that was still undergoing legislative procedures. Citizens and other officials stated their intention to file a lawsuit<ref name="dulkiewicz_news" /><ref name="sosnowiec_president_news" /><ref name="TVN24_news" /> to the prosecutor's office about the possibility of crimes being committed by the government-run Poczta Polska and by the politicians responsible for the regulation.<ref name="TVN24_news" />

===Electoral cards leakage===
On 29 April 2020, 11 days before the planned election date, election candidate [[Stanisław Żółtek]] presented a copy of an electoral ballot at a press conference.<ref name="rmf24_news">{{cite news|author=Patryk Michalski|date=30 April 2020|title=Wyciekł pakiet do głosowania w wyborach kopertowych. Poczta Polska zawiadomiła ABW.|url=https://www.rmf24.pl/raporty/raport-wybory-prezydenckie2020/najnowsze-fakty/news-wyciekl-pakiet-do-glosowania-w-wyborach-kopertowych-poczta-p,nId,4469329|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200502095153/https://www.rmf24.pl/raporty/raport-wybory-prezydenckie2020/najnowsze-fakty/news-wyciekl-pakiet-do-glosowania-w-wyborach-kopertowych-poczta-p,nId,4469329|archive-date=2 May 2020|access-date=2 May 2020}}</ref><ref name="woborcza_news_elections">{{cite news|author1=Agnieszka Kublik |author2=Wojciech Czuchnowski|date=30 April 2020|title=Wyciek kart do głosowania to prawdziwa kompromitacja pseudowyborów|url=https://wyborcza.pl/7,75398,25911286,wyciek-kart-do-glosowania-to-prawdziwa-kompromitacja-pseudowyborow.html|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200502095506/https://wyborcza.pl/7,75398,25911286,wyciek-kart-do-glosowania-to-prawdziwa-kompromitacja-pseudowyborow.html|archive-date=2 May 2020|access-date=2 May 2020}}</ref> The copies contained the names of all the candidates and other forms to be filled by voters. Żółtek said that he received the ballots from workers of one of the companies that was printing and preparing electoral documents. Poczta Polska notified the [[Internal Security Agency]] about the leak. As of 2 May 2020, Polish law did not authorise Poczta Polska to organise postal voting except in a small number of special cases.<ref name="rmf24_news" />

===Presidential election boycott===
On 30 April 2020, three former Polish [[List of heads of state of Poland#Republic of Poland (1989–present)|presidents]] and six [[List of prime ministers of Poland#Prime ministers of the Republic of Poland (1989–present)|prime ministers]] called for a boycott of 2020 presidential election, on the grounds that the election would be unconstitutional and could not guarantee the confidentiality of voters.<ref name="nytimes_news">{{cite news |author=Joanna Plucinska |date=30 April 2020 |title=Former Polish Presidents, PMs Call for Presidential Election Boycott |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/world/former-polish-presidents-pms-call-for-presidential-election-boycott-idUSKBN22C30P/ |access-date=2 May 2020 |website=reuters.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://dziennikbaltycki.pl/wybory-2020-byli-prezydenci-i-premierzy-zapowiedzieli-bojkot-majowych-wyborow-korespondencyjnych/ar/c15-14946616 |title=Wybory 2020. Byli prezydenci i premierzy zapowiedzieli bojkot majowych wyborów korespondencyjnych |publisher=Dziennik Bałtycki |date=2020-04-30 |access-date=2020-05-15}}</ref>

===Election day change===
On 6 May, [[Jarosław Gowin]], the leader of Agreement, and [[Jarosław Kaczyński]], the leader of Law and Justice struck an agreement to move the election.<ref>{{cite web|title=Nie będzie rozłamu w Zjednoczonej Prawicy. Oświadczenie Gowina i Kaczyńskiego|url=https://www.msn.com/pl-pl/wiadomosci/polska/nie-b%C4%99dzie-roz%C5%82amu-w-zjednoczonej-prawicy-o%C5%9Bwiadczenie-gowina-i-kaczy%C5%84skiego/ar-BB13HVrY?ocid=msedgntp|website=msn.com|access-date=2020-05-06}}</ref> The two parties had earlier been engaged in a political struggle over whether the election should proceed in May.<ref>{{cite web|title=Jak zagłosuje Porozumienie? Gowin spotkał się z Kaczyńskim, rozłam wśród posłów|url=https://www.msn.com/pl-pl/wiadomosci/polska/jak-zag%C5%82osuje-porozumienie-gowin-spotka%C5%82-si%C4%99-z-kaczy%C5%84skim-roz%C5%82am-w%C5%9Br%C3%B3d-pos%C5%82%C3%B3w/ar-BB13CF6e?ocid=msedgntp|website=msn.com|access-date=2020-05-06}}</ref>

On 7 May, the Sejm approved legislation for the election to be held via postal ballot.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Goclowski |first1=Marcin |title=Polish parliament approves postal vote for presidential election |url=https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-poland-election-date/polish-parliament-approves-postal-vote-for-presidential-election-idUKKBN22J0OI |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200515041147/https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-poland-election-date/polish-parliament-approves-postal-vote-for-presidential-election-idUKKBN22J0OI |url-status=dead |archive-date=15 May 2020 |publisher=Reuters |date=7 May 2020}}</ref> The same day, [[National Electoral Commission (Poland)|PKW]] announced that "The current legal regulation deprived the National Electoral Commission of the instruments necessary to perform its duties. In connection with the above, the National Electoral Commission informs voters, election committees, candidates, election administration and local government units that voting on 10 May 2020 cannot take place."{{citation needed|date=June 2020}}

The movement of the election day was met with support<ref>{{cite web|title=Jestem pod dużym wrażeniem @Jaroslaw_Gowin. Nie wiem, czy kiedykolwiek ktoś zmusił Jarosława Kaczyńskiego do ustąpienia w tak zasadniczej dla niego sprawie. Żarty z prezesa Porozumienia są dziś akurat nie na miejscu. Dzięki niemu uniknęliśmy #koronawybory.|url=https://twitter.com/Michal_Bilewicz/status/1258164600274587650|last=Bilewicz|first=Michał|date=2020-05-06|website=@Michal_Bilewicz|language=pl|access-date=2020-05-10}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Piotr Zaremba: Sprzeciwiając się majowym wyborom, @Jaroslaw_Gowin wrócił do korzeni. Do postrzegania Polski jako wspólnoty, w której przynajmniej próbuje się negocjować racje stron.|url=https://twitter.com/rzeczpospolita/status/1258846437124837376|work=Rzeczpospolita|date=2020-05-08|language=pl|access-date=2020-05-10}}</ref> and opposition<ref>{{cite web|title=Emocjonalna konferencja Czarzastego. "Tak kończą się marzenia"|url=https://www.dorzeczy.pl/kraj/139251/emocjonalna-konferencja-czarzastego-tak-koncza-sie-marzenia.html|date=2020-05-07|website=Do Rzeczy|language=pl|access-date=2020-05-10}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Wpolityce.pl|url=https://wpolityce.pl/polityka/499346-wybory-jak-najszybciej-sie-da|access-date=2020-05-10|archive-date=10 May 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200510141419/https://wpolityce.pl/polityka/499346-wybory-jak-najszybciej-sie-da|url-status=dead}}</ref> from both the "anti" and "pro" Law and Justice spheres of Polish politics. An opinion poll for [[Rzeczpospolita (newspaper)|Rzeczpospolita]] gauged public support for the Gowin-Kaczyński agreement at 43.5%, with 36.3% being against, and the rest undecided.<ref>{{cite web|title=Sondaż: Wyborcy PiS cieszą się z kompromisu. Partyjne jastrzębie - nie|url=https://www.rp.pl/Wybory-prezydenckie-2020/200519980-Wyborcy-PiS-ciesza-sie-z-kompromisu-partyjne-jastrzebie---nie.html|website=rp.pl|language=pl|access-date=2020-05-10}}</ref>

===Judgment of WSA court===
On 15 September 2020, the [[:pl:Wojewódzki sąd administracyjny|Voivodship Administrative Court]] in Warsaw judged that the decision of Prime Minister [[Mateusz Morawiecki]] to hold the May elections exclusively through mail-in voting was "[a] gross violation of the law and was issued without [legal] grounds" and violated article 7 of the [[Polish Constitution]], article 157, paragraph 1 and article 187, paragraph 1 and 2 of the Electoral Code.<ref name="WSA_judged_15sept">{{cite news|title = Sąd uchylił decyzję premiera w sprawie wyborów kopertowych. "Rażąco narusza prawo, wydana bezpodstawnie"|url = https://tvn24.pl/polska/wybory-10-maja-2020-decyzja-premiera-mateusza-morawieckiego-niewazna-wyrok-wojewodzkiego-sadu-administracyjnego-4692620|date = 15 September 2020|website = tvn24.pl|archive-url = https://archive.today/20200915093345/https://tvn24.pl/polska/wybory-10-maja-2020-decyzja-premiera-mateusza-morawieckiego-niewazna-wyrok-wojewodzkiego-sadu-administracyjnego-4692620|url-status = live|archive-date = 15 September 2020|access-date = 15 September 2020}}</ref> The opposition demanded Morawiecki's resignation.<ref name="opposition_demands_15sept">{{cite news|title = "Oczekujemy dymisji premiera". Opozycja po wyroku ws. wyborów 10 maja|url = https://www.polsatnews.pl/wiadomosc/2020-09-15/oczekujemy-dymisji-premiera-opozycja-po-wyroku-ws-wyborow-10-maja/?ref=aside_najnowsze|date = 15 September 2020|website = [[polsatnews.pl]]|archive-url = https://archive.today/20200915130733/https://www.polsatnews.pl/wiadomosc/2020-09-15/oczekujemy-dymisji-premiera-opozycja-po-wyroku-ws-wyborow-10-maja/?ref=aside_najnowsze|url-status = live|archive-date = 15 September 2020|access-date = 15 September 2020}}</ref>

