===Law and Justice / United Right===
Incumbent President [[Andrzej Duda]] was eligible to run for a second term. On 24 October 2019, in an open letter to the elected members of the Sejm and Senate, [[Law and Justice (Poland)|PiS]] chairman [[Jarosław Kaczyński]] announced that the party will strongly support Andrzej Duda in next year's presidential election.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvp.info/45001985/kaczynski-zwyciestwo-w-wyborach-trzeba-przypieczetowac-reelekcja-andrzeja-dudy|title=Kaczyński: Zwycięstwo w wyborach trzeba przypieczętować reelekcją Andrzeja Dudy|trans-title=[[Jarosław Kaczyński|Kaczyński]]: Victory in the elections must be sealed with the re-election of Andrzej Duda|work=wiadomosci.wp.pl|access-date=29 October 2019|date=24 October 2019}}</ref>

===Civic Platform / Civic Coalition===
{{Main|2019 Civic Platform presidential primary}}
[[Donald Tusk]] was widely expected to make a comeback in Polish politics and to run for President, all the more so given that his European office expired at the end of 2019.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.parlamentarny.pl/badania-opinii-i-rankingi/wybory-prezydenckie-w-2020-r-czy-donald-tusk-ma-szanse-wygrac,3691.html|title=Wybory prezydenckie w 2020 r. Czy Donald Tusk ma szansę wygrać?|trans-title=Will Donald Tusk have a chance to win the 2020 presidential elections?|work=Parlamentarny.pl|access-date=28 March 2017|date=29 December 2015|archive-date=29 March 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170329051035/http://www.parlamentarny.pl/badania-opinii-i-rankingi/wybory-prezydenckie-w-2020-r-czy-donald-tusk-ma-szanse-wygrac,3691.html|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.wprost.pl/kraj/10052383/Schetyna-Marzy-mi-sie-zeby-Donald-Tusk-byl-kandydatem-na-prezydenta-koalicji-rzadzacej.html|title=Schetyna: Marzy mi się, żeby Donald Tusk był kandydatem na prezydenta koalicji rządzącej|date=2017-04-26|work=wprost.pl|access-date=2017-10-07|trans-title="[[Grzegorz Schetyna|Schetyna]]: I dream of [[Donald Tusk]] being the ruling coalition's presidential candidate"}}</ref> However, in November 2019, he announced he would not run for the Polish presidency, citing that he has "a bag of difficult, unpopular decisions since prime minister" that would burden his candidacy. He is said to have been advised against a run by private opinion polls. He decided to run instead for the leadership of the [[European People's Party]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.politico.eu/article/donald-tusk-elected-president-of-european-peoples-party/|title=Donald Tusk elected president of European People's Party|last=de La Baume|first=Maïa |date=2019-11-20|website=POLITICO|access-date=2019-11-28}}</ref> As a result, party leader [[Grzegorz Schetyna]] decided to hold a convention in order to nominate a candidate for president. The [[2019 Civic Platform presidential primary|primary]] was won by [[Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvn24.pl/r/983976|title=Civic Platform's Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska confirms her 2020 presidential bid|website=TVN24.pl|access-date=2019-11-28}}{{Dead link|date=July 2020 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{cite web|url=http://wiadomosci.gazeta.pl/wiadomosci/7,114884,25512314,znamy-kandydata-po-na-prezydenta-przeciwko-andrzejowi-dudzie.html|title=Znamy kandydata PO na prezydenta. Do pojedynku z Andrzejem Dudą stanie Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska|website=gazetapl|date=14 December 2019 |language=pl|access-date=2019-12-14}}</ref>

Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska resigned her candidacy on 15 May 2020 under pressure of falling poll numbers and her own party.<ref name="rmf24.pl">{{cite web|title=Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska rezygnuje ze startu w wyborach prezydenckich|url=https://www.rmf24.pl/raporty/raport-wybory-prezydenckie2020/najnowsze-fakty/news-malgorzata-kidawa-blonska-rezygnuje-ze-startu-w-wyborach-pre,nId,4497121|website=rmf24.pl|language=pl|access-date=2020-05-15}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Oficjalnie: Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska rezygnuje z udziału w wyborach prezydenckich {{!}} Tysol.pl|url=https://www.tysol.pl/a48034-Oficjalnie-Malgorzata-Kidawa-Blonska-rezygnuje-z-udzialu-w-wyborach-prezydenckich|website=tysol.pl|date=15 May 2020 |language=pl|access-date=2020-05-15}}</ref> After this, [[Rafał Trzaskowski]] became the new candidate of the Civic Coalition.<ref name="scislowska1">{{cite web |title=Warsaw mayor is opposition candidate for Poland's president |url=https://www.thetelegraph.com/news/article/Main-opposition-candidate-leaves-Poland-s-15271866.php |last=Scislowska |first=Monika |agency=[[Associated Press]] |date=2020-05-15 |website=Alton Telegraph |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200530192437/https://www.thetelegraph.com/news/article/Main-opposition-candidate-leaves-Poland-s-15271866.php |access-date=2020-05-15|archive-date=30 May 2020 }}</ref> He managed to receive over 1.6 million signatures, securing his eligibility to run in the election.<ref>{{cite news |date=2020-06-09 |title=Signatures pour in for Polish presidential challenger |publisher=Reuters |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/poland-election-trzaskowski-idINKBN23G1SW|access-date=2020-06-19}}</ref> After receiving 30.46% of the vote in the first round he was defeated by the incumbent Andrzej Duda in the second round, winning 48.97% of the vote.

