==Reactions==
After voting had ended, Andrzej Duda invited Rafał Trzaskowski to the Presidential Palace to "shake hands" and "end the campaign". Trzaskowski rejected and said that they could meet after announcing the official election results.<ref>{{cite web |title=Duda zaprasza do Pałacu Prezydenckiego. Trzaskowski: to dobry pomysł, ale nie dziś |url=https://tvn24.pl/wybory-prezydenckie-2020/wybory-prezydenckie-2020-andrzej-duda-zaprasza-rafala-trzaskowskiego-do-palacu-prezydenckiego-trzaskowski-dobry-pomysl-ale-nie-dzis-4635788 |access-date=2020-07-13 |website=TVN24|date=12 July 2020 }}</ref> The next day, Trzaskowski congratulated Duda on his victory.<ref>{{cite tweet |title=Prawie 10 mln głosów. Za wszystkie i za każdy z osobna serdecznie dziękuję. Dziękuję też za niesamowitą energię, jaką wspólnie udało nam się wyzwolić przez tych kilka tygodni. Jeszcze będzie przepięknie! Gratuluję wygranej @AndrzejDuda Oby ta kadencja była rzeczywiście inna.|user=trzaskowski_ |number=1282646136583606272 |date=13 July 2020 |access-date=2020-07-13 |website=Twitter}}</ref>

[[President of the United States|US President]] [[Donald Trump]],<ref>{{cite tweet|user=realdonaldtrump|first=Donald J.|last=Trump|number=1282814301452095489|title=Congratulations to my friend President @AndrzejDuda of Poland on his historic re-election!|date=2020-07-13|access-date=2020-07-13}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-poland-election-trump-idUSKCN24E32E|title=Trump congratulates Polish President Duda's 'historic' re-election|newspaper=Reuters |date=13 July 2020|via=www.reuters.com}}</ref> [[President of the European Commission]] [[Ursula von der Leyen]],<ref>{{cite tweet |title=Congratulations to @AndrzejDuda for his reelection as President of 🇵🇱 Poland and look forward to working with him on the many challenges Europe and Poland have to face together. |user=vonderleyen |number=1282686488812060673 |date=13 July 2020 |access-date=2020-07-13 |website=Twitter}}</ref> [[NATO Secretary General]] [[Jens Stoltenberg]],<ref name="thefirstnews.com">{{cite web |url=https://www.thefirstnews.com/article/foreign-leaders-congratulate-president-duda-on-reelection-14102 |title=Foreign leaders congratulate President Duda on reelection |access-date=14 July 2020 |archive-date=13 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230113130629/https://www.thefirstnews.com/article/foreign-leaders-congratulate-president-duda-on-reelection-14102 |url-status=dead }}</ref> [[Lega Nord]] leader and former [[Italian Minister of the Interior]] [[Matteo Salvini]],<ref name="auto">{{cite tweet |title=Congratulations to my friend @AndrzejDuda on winning the Polish presidential election for the second term! I wish you strength & success. Looking forward to continuing 🇱🇹 & 🇵🇱 close cooperation in security, defence and implementing regional infrastructure projects. |user=gitanasnauseda |number=1282601506810847233 |date=13 July 2020 |access-date=2020-07-13 |website=Twitter}}</ref> [[President of Lithuania|Lithuanian President]] [[Gitanas Nausėda]],<ref name="auto"/> [[Prime Minister of the United Kingdom|UK Prime Minister]] [[Boris Johnson]],<ref>{{cite tweet |title=Congratulations to @AndrzejDuda on your re-election as President of Poland. The UK and Poland have a long, shared history and friendship in Europe, NATO and elsewhere. I look forward to that continuing as we face the challenges and opportunities ahead. |user=borisjohnson |number=1282745041593806855 |date=13 July 2020 |access-date=2020-07-13 |website=Twitter}}</ref> [[Prime Minister of Hungary|Hungarian Prime Minister]] [[Viktor Orbán]],<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-poland-election-hungary-reaction-idUSKCN24E10A|title=Hungarian government congratulates Duda on Polish election victory|newspaper=Reuters |date=13 July 2020|via=www.reuters.com}}</ref><ref name="2ndTerm">{{Cite web|url=https://apnews.com/ac1cb7dee8d5a52ae56689cedeca7018|title=Polish president wins 2nd term after bitter campaign|date=13 July 2020|website=AP NEWS}}</ref> [[President of the Czech Republic|Czech President]] [[Miloš Zeman]],<ref name="2ndTerm"/> [[President of Slovakia|Slovak President]] [[Zuzana Čaputová]],<ref name="thefirstnews.com"/> and [[President of Ukraine|Ukrainian president]] [[Volodymyr Zelenskyy]]<ref>{{cite tweet |title=Щиро вітаю пана Президента @AndrzejDuda з перемогою на виборах! Бажаю Польщі під Вашим керівництвом подальших успіхів і процвітання. Запрошую Вас відвідати Україну з візитом для продовження нашої плідної співпраці. Разом ми сильніші! |user=zelenskyyua |number=1282568060709343232 |date=13 July 2020 |access-date=2020-07-13 |website=Twitter}}</ref> congratulated Duda on his victory.

Observers viewed the election results as illustrating a divided Polish society. They also predicted that PiS would continue pursuing its policies in a number of areas and clashing with the EU.<ref name="2ndTerm"/><ref>{{cite web | last1=Plucinska | first1=Joanna | last2=Goclowski | first2=Marcin | title=Polish conservative Duda re-elected president, deeper EU rifts likely | url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-poland-election/polish-conservative-duda-re-elected-president-deeper-eu-rifts-likely-idUSKCN24E0CT | date=13 July 2020 | work=[[Reuters]] | access-date=14 July 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | last1=Wanat | first1=Zosia | title=4 takeaways from Duda's reelection as Polish president | url=https://www.politico.eu/article/4-takeaways-from-andrzej-duda-reelection-as-poland-president-result-2020/ | date=13 July 2020 | work=[[Politico]] | access-date=14 July 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | last1=Wanat | first1=Zosia | title=Poland's Duda secures another 5 years as president | url=https://www.politico.eu/article/duda-wins-polish-presidential-election-preliminary-result/ | date=13 July 2020 | work=[[Politico]] | access-date=14 July 2020}}</ref> Duda performed strongest among older, rural, low educated and [[Poland A and B|eastern]] voters.<ref>{{cite web | last1=Hirsch | first1=Cornelius | title=Poland's presidential election – by the numbers | url=https://www.politico.eu/article/poland-presidential-election-by-the-numbers-pis-law-and-justice-andrzej-duda-rafal-trzaskowski/ | date=14 July 2020 | work=[[Politico]] | access-date=14 July 2020}}</ref>

In February 2025, Mateusz Morawiecki was charged with abuse of power over his decision to hold the election solely by postal ballot when he was prime minister.<ref>{{Cite news |date=27 February 2025 |title=A former Polish prime minister is charged with exceeding his powers over a 2020 election call |language=en-US |url=https://apnews.com/article/poland-morawiecki-power-election-pandemic-charges-votes-286e5a89c94c3beda315f262377fc5c7 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250228102113/https://apnews.com/article/poland-morawiecki-power-election-pandemic-charges-votes-286e5a89c94c3beda315f262377fc5c7 |archive-date=28 February 2025 |url-status=live |access-date=27 February 2025}}</ref>

===Results challenged===
The Civic Platform party challenged results of the elections to the Polish Supreme Court, alleging irregularities and biased coverage by the state television. The appeal includes complaints from 2,000 people, containing accusations of problems with voter registry, ballot papers not being sent in time as well as issues with voting abroad. The TVP public broadcaster did not broadcast a single meeting of Trzaskowski with voters.<ref name="twitter_Robert_Klonowski_firstpost">{{cite news|date=4 July 2020|title=(Tweet)|website=Twitter|url=https://twitter.com/r_klonowski/status/1279406256214720513|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200707131930/https://twitter.com/r_klonowski/status/1279406256214720513|archive-date=7 July 2020|quote=Trzy telewizje informacyjne. Dwóch kandydatów. Transmisje. Cześć 2|access-date=3 August 2020}}</ref><ref name="twitter_Robert_Klonowski_secondpost">{{cite news|date=10 July 2020|title=(Tweet)|website=Twitter|url=https://twitter.com/r_klonowski/status/1281577026420461570|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200803173714/https://twitter.com/r_klonowski/status/1281577026420461570|archive-date=3 August 2020|quote=Trzy telewizje informacyjne. Dwóch kandydatów. Transmisje. Część 9|access-date=3 August 2020}}</ref><ref name="twitter_Robert_Klonowski_thirdpost">{{cite news|date=10 July 2020|title=(Tweet)|website=Twitter|url=https://twitter.com/r_klonowski/status/1281668661523120128|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200803173653/https://twitter.com/r_klonowski/status/1281668661523120128|archive-date=3 August 2020|quote=7 dni. 37 przykładów (kilka mi umknęło). @PolsatNewsPL i @tvn24 transmitowały wszystkie wystąpienia obu kandydatów. @tvp_info też wszystkie. Ale tylko jednego. Drugiego żadnego. Przekaz @WiadomosciTVP pomijam. A wybory już w niedzielę. Do zobaczenia przy urnach. Dobrego weekendu.|access-date=3 August 2020}}</ref>{{better source needed|date=August 2020}} Press.pl, a media-monitoring service, found that, between 3 and 16 June, nearly 97% of Wiadomości news stories devoted to Duda were positive while almost 87% of those on Trzaskowski were negative.<ref name="press_elections_news">{{cite news|date=19 July 2020|title=press.pl|website=press.pl|url=https://www.press.pl/tresc/62151,_wiadomosci_-tvp-o-rafale-trzaskowskim-tylko-negatywnie|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200803174751/https://www.press.pl/tresc/62151,_wiadomosci_-tvp-o-rafale-trzaskowskim-tylko-negatywnie|archive-date=3 August 2020|quote="Wiadomości" o Trzaskowskim źle albo wcale|access-date=3 August 2020}}</ref>

The Supreme Court ruled the election valid,<ref>{{Cite web|title=Jest decyzja Sądu Najwyższego ws. ważności wyborów prezydenckich|url=https://www.msn.com/pl-pl/wiadomosci/wybory-prezydenckie/jest-decyzja-s%C4%85du-najwy%C5%BCszego-ws-wa%C5%BCno%C5%9Bci-wybor%C3%B3w-prezydenckich/ar-BB17vgjT?ocid=msedgntp|access-date=2020-08-03|website=msn.com}}</ref> stating that doubts about the television's honesty notwithstanding, TVP was not the only media source available for voters, and that voters were free to choose what media to watch.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ponad 4 tys. protestów wyborczych ws. TVP bez dalszego biegu. "Nie spełniły warunków"|url=https://www.tokfm.pl/Tokfm/7,117303,26172913,ponad-4-tys-protestow-wyborczych-ws-tvp-bez-dalszego-biegu.html|access-date=2020-08-03|website=gazetapl|date=31 July 2020 |language=pl}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Deja|first=Maciej|date=2020-07-31|title=Sąd Najwyższy. 4086 protestów wyborczych ws. stronniczości TVP bez dalszego biegu|url=https://wiadomosci.wp.pl/sad-najwyzszy-4086-protestow-wyborczych-ws-stronniczosci-tvp-bez-dalszego-biegu-6537970829191297a|access-date=2020-08-03|website=wiadomosci.wp.pl|language=pl}}</ref>

===Office for Democratic Institutions and Human Rights report===
The [[OSCE]]'s [[Office for Democratic Institutions and Human Rights]] investigated the election and found that it was "administered professionally despite the lack of legal clarity." The ODIHR also reported that the presidential campaign "was characterized by negative and intolerant rhetoric further polarizing an already adversarial political environment. [...] the [[Telewizja Polska|TVP]] [public broadcaster] failed in its legal duty to provide balanced and impartial coverage. Instead, it acted as a campaign vehicle for the incumbent and frequently portrayed his main challenger as a  threat to Polish values and national interests. Some of the reporting was charged with xenophobic and anti-Semitic undertones."<ref name=ODIHR>{{cite report|url=https://www.osce.org/files/f/documents/4/9/455728.pdf|publisher=[[ODIHR]] Special Election Assessment Mission|title=Republic of Poland –Presidential Election, 28 June 2020 Statement of Preliminary Findings and Conclusions|date=29 June 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Pronczuk |first1=Monika |title=Poland's Supreme Court Declares Presidential Election Valid |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/03/world/europe/poland-court-presidential-election.html |access-date=31 August 2020 |work=The New York Times |date=3 August 2020}}</ref>

